# A lookup that comes, whatever the program does, to a built-in holder whose location under the name is locked finds the member there, so it does not answer undefined.
# It may come to the end of a chain where null may have been put above an object, it may meet an accessor without a getter on an object on which an accessor is defined, and a name that no holder has is not found
